a","sessionId":"4a135ea5-3967-4256-a28b-a2cb316c94af","content":"The remote check will inspect only JI Compose containers/images and report filenames, hashes, permissions, platform, and redacted failure classes. It will not print environment values, bootstrap material, or unrelated Docker state.","startedSeq":4266,"endedSeq":4307,"startedAt":"1788660704Z","endedAt":"1788660705Z","timing":{"sessionElapsedSeconds":5685,"revision":4307,"observedAt":"1788660705Z","activeTurnStartedAt":"1788655020Z","activeTurnLastActivityAt":"1788660705Z","paused":false,"reason":"active","stateSnapshot":{"elapsedSeconds":0,"activeTurnStartedAt":1788655020,"activeTurnLastActivityAt":1788660705,"revision":4307,"sawTurn":true,"pendingPermissionIds":[],"pendingElicitationIds":[],"userWaitStartedAt":null,"userWaitSeconds":0}},"raw":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_message_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"."},"messageId":"resp_08869ea15ba69143016a9ccbd1b7d087d0914a46fb0babaa4a","_meta":{"goldBandConversation":{"branchId":"root","launchedAgentExecutionId":null,"toolName":null,"toolOutput":null}}}},{"id":"activity-4308","seq":4308,"timestamp":"1788660705Z","kind":"activitySummary","startedSeq":4308,"endedSeq":4338,"startedAt":"1788660705Z","endedAt":"1788660783Z","raw":{"goldBandActivity":{"activityStartSeq":4308,"activityEndSeq":4338,"totalEventCount":6,"toolCallCount":3,"thoughtCount":3,"errorCount":0,"readFileCount":0,"writtenFileCount":0,"detailAvailable":true}}},{"id":"assistant-message-root-resp_04407b24400a6d41016a9ccc18c3fc87d0bb1ea619fb37a829","seq":4421,"timestamp":"1788660783Z","kind":"textDelta","sessionId":"4a135ea5-3967-4256-a28b-a2cb316c94af","content":"Two independent deployment defects are now evidenced, both within existing Stage 5 packaging scope: the Relay JAR is intact, but the configured bind directory is root-owned and not writable by UID 10001; the read-only Web container also tries to create an undeclared writable Nginx path. I’m isolating exact paths and testing the image under its declared UID before choosing the minimum Compose/Dockerfile correction.","startedSeq":4339,"endedSeq":4421,"startedAt":"1788660783Z","endedAt":"1788660784Z","timing":{"sessionElapsedSeconds":5764,"revision":4421,"observedAt":"1788660784Z","activeTurnStartedAt":"1788655020Z","activeTurnLastActivityAt":"1788660784Z","paused":false,"reason":"active","stateSnapshot":{"elapsedSeconds":0,"activeTurnStartedAt":1788655020,"activeTurnLastActivityAt":1788660784,"revision":4421,"sawTurn":true,"pendingPermissionIds":[],"pendingElicitationIds":[],"userWaitStartedAt":null,"userWaitSeconds":0}},"raw":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_message_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"."},"messageId":"resp_04407b24400a6d41016a9ccc18c3fc87d0bb1ea619fb37a829","_meta":{"goldBandConversation":{"branchId":"root","launchedAgentExecutionId":null,"toolName":null,"toolOutput":null}}}},{"id":"activity-4424","seq":4424,"timestamp":"1788660787Z","kind":"activitySummary","startedSeq":4424,"endedSeq":4537,"startedAt":"1788660787Z","endedAt":"1788660970Z","raw":{"goldBandActivity":{"activityStartSeq":4424,"activityEndSeq":4537,"totalEventCount":22,"toolCallCount":18,"thoughtCount":4,"errorCount":0,"readFileCount":6,"writtenFileCount":0,"detailAvailable":true}}},{"id":"assistant-message-root-resp_0aa6e6df14be0779016a9cccc06c9c87d08a66cfa981a95eaa","seq":4644,"timestamp":"1788660970Z","kind":"textDelta","sessionId":"4a135ea5-3967-4256-a28b-a2cb316c94af","content":"The root cause is precise: `/tmp` is intentionally mounted `noexec`, so Xerial can find the embedded `.so` but cannot load the extracted copy; its terminal exception is therefore misleading. The correct boundary is to extract the pinned Linux native into the immutable image and point Xerial there, while keeping `/tmp` non-executable. Separately, the one-click deployment will use a Compose-owned named metadata volume initialized with UID 10001 ownership, and Nginx will get only its required `/tmp` tmpfs.","startedSeq":4538,"endedSeq":4644,"